    "problem_statement": "Table.insert() returns -1 instead of document ID\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `insert()` method is returning -1 instead of the actual document ID that was inserted. This affects all insert operations and breaks functionality that depends on getting the correct document ID back.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom tinydb import TinyDB\nfrom tinydb.storages import MemoryStorage\n\n# Create a database\ndb = TinyDB(storage=MemoryStorage)\n\n# Insert a document - should return the document ID\ndoc_id = db.insert({'name': 'John', 'age': 30})\nprint(f\"Returned ID: {doc_id}\")  # Expected: 1, Actual: -1\n\n# Insert another document\ndoc_id2 = db.insert({'name': 'Jane', 'age': 25})\nprint(f\"Returned ID: {doc_id2}\")  # Expected: 2, Actual: -1\n\n# This also affects upsert operations\nresult = db.upsert({'name': 'Bob', 'age': 35}, db.where('name') == 'Bob')\nprint(f\"Upsert result: {result}\")  # Expected: [3], Actual: [-1]\n```\n\nThe insert method should return the actual document ID that was assigned to the inserted document, but it's consistently returning -1 instead."
  },
